<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:41Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>AI-assisted dying? Doris Dörrie's new film addresses prospect of care robots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a26e8e8f090f7c44f0276fc7e2d9f7b687f370d5acf4f95476815486592055eb</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-d_rrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715--50ff40522ded.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ai-assisted-dying-doris-dörrie-s-new-film-addresses-prospect-of-care-robots/a-79659715?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the world debates the dangers of artificial intelligence, filmmaker Doris Dörrie explores how humanoid robots could change the way we deal with aging, caregiving and how people choose to die.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Hamburg court jails 2 men over plot to attack Jewish leaders on behalf of Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e030194197839787ef15c8c086278f993befeec88e69693a6cd721de0b7d31d0</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hamburg-court-jails-2-men-over-plot-to-attack-jewish-leaders-on-behalf-of-iran/a-79667895--ad75d24ae5e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hamburg-court-jails-2-men-over-plot-to-attack-jewish-leaders-on-behalf-of-iran/a-79667895?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The men were found guilty of espionage and attempted murder. According to the court, they planned to attack the president of the Central Council of Jews in Germany and president of the German-Israeli society.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Train station alcohol ban comes into force</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c1e1d06f52001e0f4083a620db33980470799753df9ca021418e151df8c640e</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807--e7db446fe401.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-train-station-alcohol-ban-comes-into-force/live-79666807?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Consuming alcohol is no longer permitted at train stations in Germany, to improve the lot of travelers and staff alike. Coalition talks are restarting in Berlin, and an inmate is loose in Essen. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merz attacks extremes for fueling division</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a6558350d5966a105c4c1ef5fc6a947f830dec40b25747075160a70ab5713e5</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-sets-out-eu-priorities-after-urging-reforms/live-79656436--ba515100a40c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merz-attacks-extremes-for-fueling-division/live-79656436?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz accuses the far-right AfD and the socialist Left Party of deliberately fueling division and seeking political advantage from chaos.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Resignation of Bärbel Bas shines light on harsh era of German politics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6f888e66d991584636e855832edceea23e28b31d53d6d5413575c04f8ccd9ee</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:57:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T13:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-b_rbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395--56c0e1283306.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/resignation-of-bärbel-bas-shines-light-on-harsh-era-of-german-politics/a-79671395?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Labor Minister Bärbel Bas has stepped down, citing her need to grieve a loved one and leave behind the harsh realities of government. So how did German politics get so heated?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands of German gamblers could sue for their money back</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47bf3753f99056973b4f8cee670b5879ed3e3eb8f244beaa28cac641c92d7d90</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844--bc7691d0e6e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/thousands-of-german-gamblers-could-sue-for-their-money-back/a-79667844?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German gamblers may finally be able to beat the house, thanks to new court rulings in the EU and in Germany. The decisions could help gambling addicts — but the legal road might be difficult.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's far-right AfD forges a pro-Russia alliance with the BSW</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ef17a2041a953c57596cc674af4656cb51671a6535fe0aa3946ec1df1d8bcb5</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-forges-a-pro-russia-alliance-with-the-bsw/a-79662413--9f342390b0ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-far-right-afd-forges-a-pro-russia-alliance-with-the-bsw/a-79662413?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In Saxony-Anhalt, the AfD and BSW are joining forces to push for negotiations with Moscow. What is driving this rapprochement?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>'Ragebait' is the 2026 German Youth Word of the Year</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:224f082c59f6fe29f2c649ce513f9dada024dbce3912240b212e6fcb1bca78ac</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-10T13:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158--c39c4c350c71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ragebait-is-the-2026-german-youth-word-of-the-year/a-79608158?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Already named the 2025 Oxford Word of the Year, "rage bait" has also been widely adopted in German slang.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Author or artificial intelligence? Literature in crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2982cfff49673da22c8690a6a13a8e5e149cbe8c5135dcf1fab0e65936f303c</id><updated>2026-10-15T19:56:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610--2ddbca94bc5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/author-or-artificial-intelligence-literature-in-crisis/a-79618610?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">AI is a hot topic at this year's Frankfurt Book Fair. An international literary scandal has raised questions about machine-generated texts.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Servers at Munich's iconic Oktoberfest call for more respect</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9eb74ecf285f2b33fdc41